fmt writes through os.Stdout, a nil @File on bare-metal by design, so Printf/Println produce no output there and the expected text is unattainable. An environment limitation, not a codegen bug: fmt.Sprintf formats every operand correctly. Hosted/VM-only test. Covers BOTH baremetal lanes: builder-comp_arm32_baremetal (this marker, LLVM) and builder-comp_native_arm32_baremetal (via OVERRIDE_MODE, run.sh).
